+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+Tool calls are checked against the schema declared by the resolved tool definition before an executor can handle input.
+
+## Registry behavior
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a response describing schema-invalid input without calling the executor; the response does not expose an invalid property value. ([validated by: rejects invalid input before invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L11))
+- Valid input, including undeclared extra properties, reaches the executor unchanged and exactly once. ([validated by: passes valid input through unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L31))
+- A function-valued tool definition is checked against the schema resolved for that execution call. ([validated by: validates each resolved function schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L49))
+- An unregistered tool name continues to throw an `Unknown tool` error. ([validated by: preserves unknown tool errors](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L66))
